IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nad-dates`
IMPORT `nad-rules`
IMPORT `nad-seat`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) -- worked cases for the questions of the person aggrieved (nad-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion
-- is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`nd` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Which version applies (ss 116, 122, 123, 126, 128)`

-- The day before the Act commenced, and the day it did (then the pre-2022 Act applies).
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 31 7 1993) FALSE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the Act does not apply: the conduct took place before 1 August 1993 (s 116)`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 8 1993) FALSE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the Act as it stood before 3 July 2023 applies (ss 122, 123); not encoded here`
-- The day before and the day of the 2022 amendments.
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 2 7 2023) FALSE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the Act as it stood before 3 July 2023 applies (ss 122, 123); not encoded here`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 3 7 2023) FALSE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `this encoding applies`
-- A pending complaint made the day before, and the day of, Part 3 of the 2025 Act (27 July 2026).
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 9 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 26 7 2026) EQUALS `this encoding applies, but your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); not encoded here`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 9 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 27 7 2026) EQUALS `this encoding applies`
-- Inciting hatred the day before, and the day of, 31 October 2025; and with an old complaint as well.
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 30 10 2025) TRUE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `this encoding applies, except that s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies, with a strict 12-month limit (s 126)`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 31 10 2025) TRUE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `this encoding applies`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 10 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies (s 126), and your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); neither is encoded here`
-- Inciting hatred on 1 September 2025, complained of the day before, and the day of, 31 October 2025: s 126(1)(a) reaches
-- only a complaint made after the commencement; before it, the old s 20A is simply the law in force.
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 9 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 10 2025) EQUALS `s 20A as it stood when you made your complaint applies, as the law then in force (s 126 reaches only complaints made on or after 31 October 2025), and your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood then (s 128); neither is encoded here`
#ASSERT `Which version of the Act applies to me` (`d` 1 9 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS `s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies (s 126), and your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); neither is encoded here`

§§ `Attributes (s 19)`

#ASSERT `Is it a protected attribute` `disability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a protected attribute` `being subjected to domestic violence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a protected attribute` `something else not listed` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Discrimination (ss 19-21, 28)`

-- An older worker passed over for promotion because of age.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `age` `work (s 31)` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Something the Act does not list: not discrimination under the Act.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `something else not listed` `work (s 31)` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside every area of Part 4: not answered.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race (including colour, descent, nationality, ethnic or national origin, being an immigrant)` `none of these areas` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A club: 29 members is not a "club" (s 4); 30 is.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `sex` `a club (s 46)` 29 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `sex` `a club (s 46)` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Refused service because of an assistance animal: disability discrimination (s 21); not for another attribute.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `disability` `goods, services and facilities (s 41)` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race (including colour, descent, nationality, ethnic or national origin, being an immigrant)` `goods, services and facilities (s 41)` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A distinction impairing equality of opportunity, and harassment, in education (s 20(1)).
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `religious belief or activity` `education (s 29)` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `religious belief or activity` `education (s 29)` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None of the heads: s 20 "includes", so not answered.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `pregnancy` `accommodation (s 38)` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Sexual harassment (s 22)`

#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a remark with sexual connotations` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a remark with sexual connotations` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `none of these` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `an act of physical intimacy` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a demand or request for sexual favours, direct or implied` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

