§§ `General exemptions (ss 21(5), 50-59)`

-- One wrapper per family of facts; the rest FALSE.
GIVEN e IS A `General exemption`, a IS AN `Attribute`, `p1` IS A BOOLEAN, `p2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`gen pair` e a `p1` `p2` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 21(5) -- no evidence produced that the animal is an assistance animal` THEN
        `Does a general exemption cover it` e a `p1` `p2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `on another basis` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    WHEN `s 50 -- a legal incapacity` THEN
        `Does a general exemption cover it` e a FALSE FALSE `p1` `p2` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `on another basis` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    WHEN `s 57 -- a special measure` THEN
        `Does a general exemption cover it` e a FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `on another basis` FALSE FALSE FALSE `p1` `p2` FALSE FALSE FALSE
    WHEN `s 58 -- accommodating a special need would be unreasonable` THEN
        `Does a general exemption cover it` e a FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `on another basis` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `p1` `p2` FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        `Does a general exemption cover it` e a FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `p1` `p1` `p1` `p1` `p1` FALSE `on another basis` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `p1`

