§§ `Can I complain (s 60 and the bars)`

`aggrieved` MEANS `the person aggrieved by the prohibited conduct`
`org` MEANS `an organisation or body, about systemic discrimination`

#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `no earlier complaint about the same conduct` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `a person authorised in writing by the Commissioner, on behalf of the person aggrieved` `no earlier complaint about the same conduct` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `someone else` `no earlier complaint about the same conduct` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Declined after assessment: no second individual complaint even with permission; a representative one with permission.
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `declined by the Commissioner after assessment (s 66)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `org` `declined by the Commissioner after assessment (s 66)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `org` `declined by the Commissioner after assessment (s 66)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `declined because no further action could be taken (s 66E)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `declined because no further action could be taken (s 66E)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `withdrawn (s 71)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `withdrawn (s 71)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lapses: no permission power (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `lapsed because I did not say I wished to continue (s 72)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `lapsed because I did not ask in time for referral to the Tribunal (s 81(6))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `aggrieved` `declined as frivolous, trivial or misconceived, or as dealt with elsewhere (ss 67, 68)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The time limit for complaining (ss 65, 126)`

#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` TRUE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 1 10 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` FALSE FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` TRUE FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026

-- The last day and the day after; the day of the conduct itself; a day before the conduct.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate (s 65(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 14 3 2026) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before the conduct`
-- s 126: inciting hatred on 1 October 2025.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2025) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2025) (`d` 2 10 2026) EQUALS `late, and the Commissioner cannot accept it (s 126(2))`
-- A representative complaint: 24 months.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` TRUE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2028) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` TRUE FALSE (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2028) EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate (s 65(2))`
-- From 29 February 2024: the last day is 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time if made on this day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate (s 65(2))`

§§ `The Commissioner's decision (s 66)`

#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the Commissioner decide on my complaint` TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 10 2026

§§ `A lapse notice (s 72)`

#ASSERT `By when must I say I wish to continue` (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `d` 31 10 2026
-- Advised on 31 December 2026: 60 days run over the end of February 2027 (not a leap year).
#ASSERT `By when must I say I wish to continue` (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `Does my complaint continue if I reply on this day` (`d` 1 9 2026) (`d` 31 10 2026) EQUALS `the complaint continues`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint continue if I reply on this day` (`d` 1 9 2026) (`d` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 72(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint continue if I reply on this day` (`d` 1 9 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `the complaint continues`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint continue if I reply on this day` (`d` 1 9 2026) (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before you were advised`

§§ `Conciliation (ss 79, 80)`

#ASSERT `What happens if I do not attend conciliation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing follows: there was no written direction, or you complied with it`
#ASSERT `What happens if I do not attend conciliation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing follows: there was no written direction, or you complied with it`
#ASSERT `What happens if I do not attend conciliation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing follows: you had a reasonable excuse (ss 79(6), 80(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I do not attend conciliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner may dismiss your complaint and direct you to pay the respondent's costs (s 80(1)(a)), and not complying is an offence with a maximum penalty of 100 penalty units (s 79(4))`
#ASSERT `s 79 -- the maximum penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 100

§§ `Referral to the Tribunal (ss 81, 86, 87)`

-- Notice received 10 November 2026: 21 days later is 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for a Tribunal hearing` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the last day to ask is` (`d` 1 12 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for a Tribunal hearing` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `the last day to ask is` (`d` 15 12 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for a Tribunal hearing` TRUE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `a representative complaint is not referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `in time: the Commissioner must refer your complaint to the Tribunal (s 87(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` (`d` 2 12 2026) EQUALS `too late: the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 81(6))`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 12 2026) (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `in time: the Commissioner must refer your complaint to the Tribunal (s 87(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 12 2026) (`d` 16 12 2026) EQUALS `too late: the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 81(6))`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` FALSE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` (`d` 9 11 2026) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before you received the notification`
#ASSERT `Is my request for a Tribunal hearing in time if made on this day` TRUE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `a representative complaint cannot be referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`

§§ `Compensation (s 88)`

-- The prescribed maximum is an input; 60000 here is an illustrative figure, not the regulation's.
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal order this compensation` TRUE 50000 60000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal order this compensation` TRUE 60000 60000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal order this compensation` TRUE 60001 60000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal order this compensation` FALSE 1000 60000 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Appeal (s 106)`

#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (`d` 1 12 2026) TRUE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `d` 29 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 17 1 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE `nd` EQUALS `d` 29 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (`d` 1 12 2026) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 29 12 2026
